@startuml
left to right direction

title Use Case Diagram for AI-Powered Analysis & Insights System

rectangle "System" {
  usecase "CFR001: View Financial Insights Dashboard" as CFR001
  usecase "SAFR001: Manage Analysis Parameters" as SAFR001
  usecase "FAFR004: Configure Analysis Parameters for Client Segments" as FAFR004
  usecase "SFR002: Deliver Personalized Recommendations Based on Financial Profiles" as SFR002
  usecase "AIFR003: Generate Spending Limit Alerts by Identifying Unusual Deviations" as AIFR003
  usecase "CFR011: Send Feedback to Improve System Outputs" as CFR011

  Client --> CFR001 : View financial data and insights in a consolidated dashboard.
  User -> (CFR002) : Receive alerts about anomalous transactions for fraud detection. 
                     'User' here refers to any client, advisor or admin who needs such notifications.

  SysAdmin -->> SAFR001: Manage system parameters ensuring compliance with regulations like Basel III and AML.
  
  FAFR004 <|-- (SAFR001): Customize analysis settings for specific client segments under GDPR/CCPA standards.  

  SFR002 --> CFR003 : Provide financial predictions based on historical data and market trends.

  Client -->> AIFR009: Receive contextualized news related to their investment portfolio.
  
  System --> AIFR001 : Request future financial predictions from the AI component.  

  User -> (CFR004) : Personalized recommendations aligned with user's goals and risk tolerance.

  Client -->> SFR003: Access historical records of insights for trend analysis.

  SysAdmin -->> CFR005: Manage personalized recommendation preferences under KYC profile.
  
  FAFR002 --> SAFR001 : View client intervention alerts generated by the system.  

  FinancialAdvisor -> (FAFR003) : Analyze clients' financial situations using predictive analytics.

  Client -->> AIFR004: Receive investment opportunity analyses based on risk profile.
  
  System -->> SFR008: Request specific investments matching user criteria and ESG preferences.  

  SysAdmin --> CFR010: Manage relationships with Financial Advisors, including data sharing permissions.
}

@enduml